AAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"flaky","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed in the same rewrite as allstar-sleepy-armadillo (Gerrit 3480, commit 2b5e23a32c0): the test no longer uses future.result(timeout=60); workers are joined without a per-worker bound and the suite's 300 s per-test budget bounds a hang. Not yet done for this ticket: a deterministic reproduction of the 60 s expiry (observed 2 of 2 serial runs at load 25-45, 203 s and 247 s wall); it stays open until that is recorded or the bug is closed against 3480 with that evidence.","timestamp":1795183889600922001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation notes after plan review. (1) Worst-case wait: write_lock defaults (timeout 30, attempts 2) give a 60 s window per pass, and write_path_retries() (default 2) gives 3 passes, so about 180 s plus jittered backoff, the same budget every canonical store write already takes. (2) _merge_ref has 3 callers: the candidate merge (a lock failure fails the close, the case reproduced here) and the 2 post-publication convergence paths (_converge_fetched_publication and the already-present path), which on a lock failure record pending local sync and return a *_local_pending result; they now wait the same canonical budget before doing so, which is intended: the remote already holds the close, and a longer wait only makes convergence more likely to finish in-process. (3) Added test_candidate_merge_waits_on_the_canonical_write_lock_budget (patches write_lock, asserts dual_window=True and retries=write_path_retries() with no fixed timeout), so a regression to timeout=10, attempts=1 fails CI. Module: 19 passed. A 4 s-per-start shim run of the race test with the fix is in progress.","timestamp":1795245730823774001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795181752771218001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eee8a8d3-f06d-4c6f-9475-79e2b142f131","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa59-9a21-097b-49be"},{"link_uuid":"f9090f58-d04f-432e-b79a-4c0b7cf92c33","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9a53-1e7c-45d6-4412"},{"link_uuid":"9e152dca-e634-4389-bdc8-26b217a0ac80","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618"}],"description":"## Observation\nOutside the agent sandbox on 2026-11-20 at about 06:00 PST (host load average 25-45 from concurrent verifies), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle` failed 2 of 2 serial runs with `concurrent.futures.TimeoutError` from `future.result(timeout=60)` (test line 401), after 247 s and 203 s of wall time.\n\n## Root cause (verified): two fixed wall-clock bounds\n1. The test's own `future.result(timeout=60)` per worker. Removed by e7532d2b71c (Gerrit 3480, allstar-sleepy-armadillo), which joins plain processes without a per-worker bound.\n2. Still live after that rewrite: `_merge_ref` in `src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py` takes the store write lock with `timeout=10, attempts=1` and no retries, unlike every canonical store write (`write_path_retries()`, default 30 s windows with 2 retry passes). When both workers close the same ticket, the one that waits gives up after a single 10 s window whenever the other holds the lock longer, which a slow host produces, and its close fails with `completion candidate merge failed: flock: could not acquire lock after 10s`. A real concurrent close on a loaded host fails the same way.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (Nov 20 2026, PATH `git` shim sleeping a fixed delay before every git start, `-o timeout=2000` so only the bounds under test can fire):\n- Before e7532d2b71c (worktree at e7532d2b71c^): `TimeoutError` at delays of 1.5 s, 2.5 s and 4 s (1 failed each).\n- At origin/main (after e7532d2b71c): `AssertionError: a commit worker raised: CommandError('Error: completion candidate merge failed: flock: could not acquire lock after 10s ...')` at 1.5 s, 2.5 s and 4 s.\n- With the change below, at 1.5 s: 1 passed (call 181.69 s).\n\n## Approach\nIn `_merge_ref`, take the lock with the canonical write-path budget, `store_lock.write_lock(tracker, dual_window=True, retries=store_lock.write_path_retries())`, the same call `event_append` uses for every store write. The merge itself is unchanged and stays under the lock; only how long a waiter waits changes. No config key, environment variable or flag is added (`write_path_retries()` is the existing resolver).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py`\n\n## Testing\n- The 1.5 s shim run of the race test: fails before (lock timeout) and passes after, both recorded on this ticket.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py` and the completion-delivery unit tests pass without a shim.\n- `make verify` through the verify slot.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A deterministic reproduction is recorded here, for both the original 60 s bound and the remaining 10 s merge-lock bound.\n- [x] Under the 1.5 s-per-start shim the race test passes with the change, and fails without it, runs recorded here.\n- [x] The completion candidate merge waits on the canonical write-path lock budget.\n- [x] `make verify` passes and Gerrit gives Verified +1. (Slot verify: only main's then-red encoding guard failed, integration 226 passed; Gerrit 3504 LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 after rebase onto the fix; merged 03e47296da0)","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py","reason":"merge lock uses the canonical write-path budget"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py","reason":"regression test pinning the merge lock budget"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9a53-1e7c-45d6-4412"],["relates_to","fa59-9a21-097b-49be"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ebc094bd-b97d-4763-8dbb-b282ee296812","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9b8a-60c3-2194-418c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Concurrent close of one ticket fails on a slow host: completion merge waits a single 10 s lock window (and the test once waited 60 s per worker)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["902da330-d08e-4580-aca9-50d55ba2f271","9719771f-618e-4581-afb6-37bdadf64bbe","bce687eb-bc38-424d-b738-04b9fcc63b68","9f63a41a-14b4-40e5-aefe-8f2a763cb06c","10a1bed4-726f-4836-b519-7d64be3ac87f","87df4368-f199-4fb0-bcbd-730f5dcedc08","14b4db16-62cf-44ab-9914-88ad8c99a4b3","f9090f58-d04f-432e-b79a-4c0b7cf92c33","6e90c824-8b03-44e7-a0eb-dc2fb3f6956e","ebc094bd-b97d-4763-8dbb-b282ee296812","bf80fc74-5969-46c0-be92-ccb5684bf694","9e152dca-e634-4389-bdc8-26b217a0ac80"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795270557113358002,"uuid":"4c6dadb1-72b6-497d-9bc6-5ab6349401ef"}